\\tau(\\nu_{\\rm pk})\\simeq\\frac{\\pi^{2}m_{p}}{1620m_{e}}f_{\\xi}\\nu_{\\rm pk}t. 

The observed FRB frequency \\nu_{\\rm max} is reached as \\tau\\simeq 3. Since \\tau(\\nu)\\propto\\nu^{-4}, we get

\\frac{\\nu_{\\rm max}}{\\nu_{\\rm pk}}\\simeq 7.81\\left(\\frac{\\tau}{3}\\right)^{-1/4}f _{\\xi,-3}^{1/4}\\left(\\frac{\\nu_{\\rm pk}}{\\rm GHz}\\right)^{1/4}t_{-3}^{1/4},  where the peak frequencies of two pulses

