Here we implicitly take \\sigma_{\\rm II}<1. The reason is that the effective maser efficiency of pulse I should not be too small since observationally the flux ratio between radio and X-ray band is F_{\\rm radio}/F_{X}\\sim 10^{-6}-10^{-5}(Mereghetti et al., 2020). The observed emission frequency is higher for pulse II and according to the waterfall plots we normalize them as \\nu_{\\rm max,I}=400 MHz, \\nu_{\\rm max,II}=1.4 GHz. Thus

